{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310748,"nonce":"ekr5nyCGLsuF5aNXr4/idg4FReo=","title":"wasm `indirect call type mismatch` trap when GenerationLoop.generate invokes its streaming callback. Surfaced 2026-06-08 after the Std.int ...","message":"**Fact:** After commits f7ae53f (anon-struct ABI) and 71ff161\n(Val::F64 from_bits), `rayzor run --wasm nue/examples/llama-chat/Main.hx`\nloads the full Llama 3.2 1B GGUF, builds the LlamaArch + KV cache +\ntokenizer, prints `[meta] llama hidden=2048 layers=16 ...`, prints\n`[tok] vocab=128256`, prints `[gen] streaming...`, then traps:\n\n```\nwasm trap: indirect call type mismatch\nwasm backtrace:\n  0:  0x422bf - \u003cunknown\u003e!\u003cwasm function 1368\u003e\n  1:  0x46578 - \u003cunknown\u003e!\u003cwasm function 1406\u003e\n```\n\nThe callsite is `loop.generate(modelPrompt, callback)` at\n`nue/examples/llama-chat/Main.hx:353`. The callback is a Haxe\nfunction literal with signature `function(_id:Int, partial:String):Bool`\nthat closes over `prevLen` and `nTokens` (single-element arrays).\n\n**Why:** Wasm `call_indirect` checks that the signature embedded in\nthe indirect call instruction matches the signature of the function\nthe table slot points at. A mismatch traps with this exact message.\nFor a Haxe closure-typed parameter the caller does\n`call_indirect \u003cfn_idx\u003e, \u003cexpected_sig\u003e`; the callee was compiled as\nsome `(env_ptr, ...) -\u003e result` shape. If the wasm backend lowered\nthe closure-receiving site (`GenerationLoop.generate`) with a\ndifferent expected_sig than the closure itself uses, every call\nthrough the callback traps.\n\nPlausible mismatches to check:\n- Env-ptr placement (first vs last arg, or omitted when expected).\n- Boxed vs unboxed primitive args (e.g. `Int` lowered to i32 vs\n  Dynamic-boxed i32 pointer at one side but not the other).\n- Return type (`Bool` lowered as i32 vs Dynamic-boxed Bool at\n  callsite vs callee).\n- The closure's `_id:Int` may be passed as i64 in one place and i32\n  in the other.\n\n**How to apply:**\n\n1. Reproducer (no GGUF needed): write a minimal Haxe sample where\n   one function takes a `(Int, String) -\u003e Bool` parameter and the\n   caller passes a closure that captures a heap-array. Build for\n   wasm, run, expect the same trap. Put it in\n   `compiler/tests/haxe/` alongside `test_anon_struct_return.hx`.\n2. Inspect both ends of the `call_indirect` lowering in\n   `compiler/src/codegen/wasm_backend.rs`:\n   - The closure construction site (where the closure's wasm function\n     index goes into the indirect table).\n   - The call site (where `call_indirect \u003ctype_idx\u003e` is emitted).\n3. Cross-check against the native cranelift backend — closures work\n   there. The diff between cranelift's lowering and wasm_backend's\n   for closure call/construction is the lever.\n\n**Status:** Top wasm blocker as of 2026-06-08 commit 71ff161. The\nload + arch + tokenizer build path is fully working. Generation loop\ntraps on first callback invocation.\n\nRelated fixes that unblocked us to reach this point:\n- [[perf_wasm_bytes_in_linear_memory_arc]] — bytes-in-linear-memory\n- f7ae53f (Codex) — anonymous-object slot ABI fix\n- 71ff161 — Std.int / Std.string Val bit-pattern decode\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_wasm_indirect_call_type_mismatch_gen` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}